"ArmorCode Platform"""		"Update the route table associated with the private subnet so that the 0.0.0.0/0 route targets the Transit Gateway as required by the architecture and remove or replace the existing 0.0.0.0/0 route that targets the NAT Gateway. If outbound internet access is still required for the workloads, implement it through the approved Transit Gateway egress pattern and any mandated inspection/egress controls. Validate that the subnet is associated with the correct route table, confirm there are no overlapping or conflicting routes, and then re-test connectivity to ensure traffic follows the Transit Gateway path while maintaining access to required internal destinations."	ics-aem-dev	https://app.wiz.io/issues#~(issue~'922387ca-360c-41ea-8ef5-eff0d599b847)	https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/vpcconsole/home?region=us-east-1#RouteTableDetails:RouteTableId=rtb-00510c48e42cff16e	"{""Name"": ""int-private-us-east-1b-rtb"", ""Owner"": ""Deepika.Sharma@broadridge.com"", ""SDLCEnv"": ""int"", ""Segment"": ""ics"", ""ArcherID"": ""2169"", ""Function"": ""Cloud Platform"", ""ECALiason"": ""rakshitha.govindannavar@broadridge.com"", ""ShortName"": ""aem"", ""ChargeCode"": ""HB035-25102-100781-132001-52000300-00000-0000-0000-Unidentified-XC AWS ADOBECX-Unidentified-0000"", ""Deployed By"": ""Cloud Foundation Architecture"", ""EstimatedCosts"": ""None"", ""bfs:aws_region"": ""us-east-1"", ""ApplicationName"": ""Adobe Campaign Classic AEM"", ""DevelopmentLead"": ""Deepika.Sharma@broadridge.com"", ""cfa:application"": ""aem"", ""cfa:internal_id"": ""f5634cb1-f6b6-421d-bf46-5c1c32858baa"", ""FinancialAnalyst"": ""Alyssa.Nunziato@broadridge.com"", ""cfa:classification"": ""npd"", ""AlertsNotificationDL"": ""BRAdobeSupport@broadridge.com"", ""ApprovedDevelopmentBudget"": ""2000""}"				rtb-00510c48e42cff16e			2026-04-24T04:49:27Z	2026-04-27T07:27:06Z							[]																						
2026-02-17T09:38:30Z	Route table has a default route (0.0.0.0/0) to a NAT Gateway - (Broadridge)	HIGH	IN_PROGRESS	"This custom rule identifies private subnets whose associated route table contains a default route (0.0.0.0/0) pointing to a NAT Gateway. In the IP network design, private subnets are expected to send all non-local traffic through a Transit Gateway to ensure centralized routing, inspection, and governance. A default route to a NAT Gateway changes the intended egress path by enabling direct internet-bound outbound connectivity for resources in the private subnet, which can bypass required centralized security controls, logging, and segmentation enforced via the Transit Gateway. This condition may indicate a subnet that is misclassified as private, an incorrect route table association, or an exception that has not been formally approved."	routetable	rtb-0d776335620982f1d	4.37E+11	"84c2a1fc-612d-5b9c-acda-6c03e2228f50, 8bbbf1d9-3245-58e7-8837-40ccbc8b4745, c6f60c1b-3c0f-50a7-b4f5-8def04c0f7e0"	"NPD, NPD-ICS, NPD-ICS-AEM"			f5a26259-62f1-5ac7-ae6e-cfc44cf73105	int-private-us-east-1a-rtb	us-east-1	Active	AWS		"{""Tags"": [{""Key"": ""ApplicationName"", ""Value"": ""Adobe Campaign Classic AEM""}, {""Key"": ""ChargeCode"", ""Value"": ""HB035-25102-100781-132001-52000300-00000-0000-0000-Unidentified-XC AWS ADOBECX-Unidentified-0000""}, {""Key"": ""EstimatedCosts"", ""Value"": ""None""}, {""Key"": ""cfa:internal_id"", ""Value"": ""f5634cb1-f6b6-421d-bf46-5c1c32858baa""}, {""Key"": ""AlertsNotificationDL"", ""Value"": ""BRAdobeSupport@broadridge.com""}, {""Key"": ""ECALiason"", ""Value"": ""rakshitha.govindannavar@broadridge.com""}, {""Key"": ""Function"", ""Value"": ""Cloud Platform""}, {""Key"": ""Segment"", ""Value"": ""ics""}, {""Key"": ""ShortName"", ""Value"": ""aem""}, {""Key"": ""Deployed By"", ""Value"": ""Cloud Foundation Architecture""}, {""Key"": ""bfs:aws_region"", ""Value"": ""us-east-1""}, {""Key"": ""ApprovedDevelopmentBudget"", ""Value"": ""2000""