2024-06-26T12:49:17Z	VPC has no Route 53 DNS resolver with logging enabled	MEDIUM	OPEN	This VPC has no Route53 DNS resolver with logging enabled. 																																							
																																											
Without logging	 you could miss early indicators of a security breach. For example	 a sudden increase in DNS requests or requests to unfamiliar domains can indicate a malware infection or an ongoing data breach. In case of a security incident	 DNS logs can provide crucial information to understand the actions taken by an attacker. Without these logs	" your ability to carry out a thorough forensic investigation might be limited."""	vpc	vpc-074b34962de19e502	4.37E+11	"84c2a1fc-612d-5b9c-acda-6c03e2228f50, 8bbbf1d9-3245-58e7-8837-40ccbc8b4745, c6f60c1b-3c0f-50a7-b4f5-8def04c0f7e0"	"NPD, NPD-ICS, NPD-ICS-AEM"			wc-id-2175	vpc-074b34962de19e502	us-west-2	Active	AWS		"{""Tags"": null, ""State"": ""available"", ""VpcId"": ""vpc-074b34962de19e502"", ""OwnerId"": ""437377876052"", ""CidrBlock"": ""172.31.0.0/16"", ""IsDefault"": true, ""DhcpOptionsId"": ""dopt-8d8fd6f5"", ""InstanceTenancy"": ""default"", ""EncryptionControl"": null, ""BlockPublicAccessStates"": {""InternetGatewayBlockMode"": ""off""}, ""CidrBlockAssociationSet"": [{""CidrBlock"": ""172.31.0.0/16"", ""AssociationId"": ""vpc-cidr-assoc-01a6605a271b601cc"", ""CidrBlockState"": {""State"": ""associated"", ""StatusMessage"": null}}], ""Ipv6CidrBlockAssociationSet"": null}"	f091d4b1-e888-4381-920c-b1429145f74b	57fda215-67b3-53f0-b6dd-8c56429d7767				Perform the following commands via AWS CLI:																			
