#NAME?																																											
"ArmorCode Platform"""		### Ensure secure use of encryption keys																																									
* Prefer customer-managed keys rather than cloud provider encryption keys. 																																											
* When using cloud provider encryption keys	 protect the principals that can access them:																																										
   * Use the ?Ç£least privilege?Ç¥ principle when assigning permissions	 meaning that each account is assigned the exact permissions that it needs to function properly. When assigning permissions	 avoid wild-card permissions.																																									
   * To find unused permissions assigned to the principal	 use the ?Ç£Excessive Permissions?Ç¥ object on the Security Graph.																																										
   * Minimize the attack surface of principals with sensitive permissions by remediating all Issues associated to them.																																											
   * Avoid using access keys. They function as long-term credentials to the principal	 and are more easily compromised.																																										
   * Enable MFA for users with sensitive permissions if possible.																																											
"* Set an expiration date for all secrets and rotate them on a regular basis."""	ics-aem-dev	https://app.wiz.io/issues#~(issue~'087585e3-86ca-418a-8ef8-3c1f89cbdd96)	https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home?region=us-east-1#/file-systems/fs-704c71c4	"{""Name"": ""aem-service-efs-storage"", ""aws:elasticfilesystem:default-backup"": ""enabled""}"				arn:aws:elasticfilesystem:us-east-1:437377876052:file-system/fs-704c71c4	INSECURE_USE_OF_SECRETS		2026-04-23T23:53:09Z	2026-04-27T11:53:16Z					"AWS Well-Architected Framework (Section 2 - Security), C5 - Cloud Computing Compliance Criteria Catalogue, CIS Controls v8.1, CRI Profile v2.0, FISC Security Guidelines, HITRUST CSF v11.2, IRS 1075, ISM (Australian Government), ISO/IEC 27001-2022, ISO/IEC 27017:2015, K-ISMS (Korean Information Security Management System), MAS Technology Risk Management Guidelines, MITRE ATT&CK Cloud Matrix, MITRE ATT&CK Matrix, NIS2 Directive (Article 21), NIST 800-171 Rev.2, NIST CSF v2.0, NYDFS (23 NYCRR 500), NZISM, PCI DSS v4.0.1, Risk Management in Technology (RMiT), SCF (Secure Controls Framework), SCF (Secure Controls Framework) 2025.4, SEBI Cybersecurity and Cyber Resilience Framework (CSCRF), SOC 2, SWIFT CSCF v2025, Telecommunications security act code of practice 2021 (TSA UK), Wiz (Legacy), Wiz for Data Security (Legacy), Wiz for Risk Assessment, Wiz for Secrets Security"	"AWS Well-Architected Framework (Section 2 - Security) - SEC 2 Identity and access management - How do you manage authentication for people and machines?, AWS Well-Architected Framework (Section 2 - Security) - SEC 8 Data protection - How do you protect your data at rest?, C5 - Cloud Computing Compliance Criteria Catalogue - 5.8 Cryptography and Key Management (CRY), CIS Controls v8.1 - 16 Application Software Security, CIS Controls v8.1 - 3 Data Protection, CRI Profile v2.0 - Protect: Data Security, FISC Security Guidelines - Practice Guidelines 1 Information security, FISC Security Guidelines - Practice Gui